ecision and its attestation argument in an ADR/design-doc update (e.g. an ADR 0005 addendum), not only in the ticket.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'code snapshots are the attestation basis for signed verdicts'","'the case ADR 0005 D2 was written for' — the reuse assumption in an existing ADR is being extended to a fast-moving regime it 'does not cover'","No AC or step names a doc/ADR update"],"finding":"The change alters how <store>/<sha> code snapshots are built, and the plan itself names these as the attestation basis for signed verdicts, but no ADR/design-doc update is planned to capture this decision (ADR 0005 D2's reuse assumption is cited as the very thing being extended).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8b55e2faf081f2b8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Why it was scoped out of 8386' and Acceptance criteria","norm_id":"n75b98d5251d88834","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future reader of ADR 0005 D2 sees the reuse assumption but not that code entries now hardlink-share, and cannot reconcile the attestation claim"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Sharpen AC line 3 to state that submodule-bearing trees fall back to full materialization by construction (gitlinks are not hardlinkable), so the delta-built-entry check need only confirm LFS-pointer detection still runs on a hardlink-cloned tree.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3067,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["delta_tree.py _LINKABLE_MODES = frozenset({'100644','100755'}); _tree_paths returns None when 'mode not in _LINKABLE_MODES' — a gitlink (160000) or symlink forces the whole-tree fail-closed fallback","docstring of delta_tree: 'a tree containing entries we cannot hardlink faithfully (symlinks, gitlinks)' is an explicit fail-closed cause","repo_snapshot.materialize populate branch computes lfs/subs via _detect_lfs_pointers(dest) + _list_submodules(root_dir, sha) AFTER the build, independent of how the tree was produced"],"finding":"AC line 3 asks that 'the submodule caveat sidecars are still computed correctly for a delta-built entry', but the generic helper it wires through (materialize_via_donor -> _tree_paths in delta_tree.py) returns None and fails closed for ANY tree whose ls-tree contains a gitlink (mode 160000) or symlink, because 160000 is not in _LINKABLE_MODES. By construction a code tree that contains a submodule can therefore NEVER be delta-built — it always falls through to the unchanged full _materialize_tree path. The AC as phrased sends the implementer to verify submodule-caveat correctness on the delta path, a case the delta path structurally excludes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe1010ff430b97d14","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, line 3 ('the LFS-pointer and submodule caveat sidecars are still computed correctly for a delta-built entry')","norm_id":"n24328945b1a3630e","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A code SHA whose tree contains a submodule gitlink is resolved: materialize_via_donor returns False, full materialization runs, and _list_submodules records the gitlink as today — the delta path is never exercised for that tree"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword AC-3 to: 'Each entry still byte-matches the committed tree at its own SHA; LFS-pointer detection is still computed correctly for a delta-built entry; and trees containing a submodule gitlink (which the donor helper cannot hardlink) fall back to full materialization, so their submodule caveat is recorded exactly as today.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State in AC1 which outcome is the default expectation (reuse) and reserve the 'record the decision not to' branch for a specific, enumerated blocking condition (e.g. attestation cannot be preserved).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'reuses unchanged blobs from a verified neighbouring code entry, or the decision not to is recorded with its reasoning'","The 'Why it was scoped out / still worth doing' section argues the fix IS worth doing, implying reuse is the intended outcome"],"finding":"AC1 offers an escape hatch ('or the decision not to is recorded with its reasoning') without stating which outcome is the expected default, leaving the core design choice partly to the executor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb75d013193aa69ac","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, first bullet","norm_id":"ne58b6417fbf5a968","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor reads AC1 and cannot tell whether skipping the reuse (and just documenting why) is an acceptable completion or a punt"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword AC1: 'materialize's populate branch reuses unchanged blobs from a verified neighbouring code entry. If — and only if — the attestation invariant (AC4) cannot be preserved under sharing, the decision not to share is recorded with its reasoning instead.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concurrency and retirement contract for cross-entry hardlinks: is donor selection + clone atomic against a concurrent acquire or eviction of the donor entry, and does removing one entry preserve the byte-integrity of neighbours that hardlink its blobs?","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5a","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'reuses unchanged blobs from a verified neighbouring code entry' — hardlinks create cross-entry shared inodes","'the cache.acquire populate branch' builds <store>/<sha> — a shared content-addressed store","ABSENCE: the plan states the algorithm is generic and 'the work is in the review and the test', but does not state whether concurrent acquires of adjacent SHAs are safe (TOCTOU: neighbour selected then mutated/deleted mid-clone) or how entry retirement interacts with hardlinked blobs"],"finding":